cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  When citing the study itself, please cite the associated article.
type: software
title: >-
  Analysis code for: Biological and Anthropometric Correlates of Sleep
  Quality in a Young-Adult University Sample
abstract: >-
  Reproducible R pipeline for a cross-sectional study of sleep quality
  (Pittsburgh Sleep Quality Index) and body composition in a young-adult
  university sample (Universidad Nacional del Callao, Peru). Covers
  de-identification, a three-stage clinical audit of the physiological
  measurements, multiple imputation by chained equations (m = 100), the
  pooled logistic-regression association model, multiple factor analysis,
  and every table and figure in the manuscript. The design is explanatory:
  associations are reported as odds ratios with 95% confidence intervals.
  No prediction model is developed or evaluated.

